            0.883,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Continue the discussion on the given reasons or conduct activities to find evidence for the reasons given to help in this discussion. Where else have you seen water droplets like this?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.092,
            0.174,
            0.432,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.092,
                0.174,
                0.432,
                0.336
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.179,
                0.342,
                0.347,
                0.358
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Dew drops on plants"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.454,
            0.166,
            0.883,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You might have seen dew drops on plants. Why do we see dew drops more in the morning? When we boil the water in a half-filled utensil and cover it with a steel plate, some water drops accumulate on the inner side of the steel plate. Where do these water drops come from? What do you think?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.451,
            0.329,
            0.883,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the water vapour present in the air comes in contact with a cold surface,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.37,
            0.882,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "it forms water droplets. The process of conversion of water vapour into its liquid state is called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "condensation",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.411,
            0.883,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "After understanding the concept of condensation of water, let us go back to Activity 8.3. Could the water appearing on the outer surface of the glass tumbler in Activity 8.3 also be due to condensation of water vapour present in the air? Let us investigate it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.525,
            0.559,
            0.546
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 8.4: Let us measure"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.556,
            0.883,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Aavi and Thirav conduct an activity to find evidence for their reasons. You can also conduct the activity by following the steps given below. Record your data in Table 8.2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.62,
            0.883,
            0.682
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Take a glass tumbler half-filled with water containing a few ice cubes. Cover it with a small steel plate. Weigh it on a digital weighing balance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.687,
            0.882,
            0.728
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Observe the reading on the balance and record the weight after every five minutes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.733,
            0.882,
            0.776
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Continue observing for 30 minutes. Record your observations in Table 8.2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.782,
            0.883,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Predict",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " what will happen to the mass of cold water kept on the digital weighing balance. Will it increase or decrease or remain the same?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 14,
